Description: drdynvc: serialize received data between the TCP and UDP threads
 The Slime OS UDP transport (slimeos-udp-transport.patch) delivers PDUs from its
 receive thread while the main thread delivers TCP data. Both used the shared
 drdynvc->data_in with no lock, which corrupted the DVC stream pool (SIGSEGV in
 StreamPool_Take on the Android build, 2026-10-04). A lock around the receive
 function makes them take turns and leaves the data path itself unchanged.
 (+slimeos12 instead gave whole PDUs a stream of their own; that made video lag
 in bursts on the AMD box, so it was dropped.)
Author: Slime OS
Forwarded: no
